1
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:09,000
NOVA Blockchain Lab was glad to bring
our game, Treasure Hunt, here to FIL.

2
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:10,500
What's the game about?

3
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:15,320
This game turns the FIL pavilion
into a huge treasure hunt,

4
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:21,360
where participants look for our tags,
tap their phone and earn points.

5
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:23,220
And points get you rewards.

6
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:24,380
How does it work?

7
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:27,080
We hide the tags
across the exhibitor stands.

8
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:29,660
These treasures are NFC tags,

9
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:35,720
so anyone who finds one just taps it
with their phone and gets the reward.

10
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:40,200
There's no need to install any app.
It's very easy to use.

11
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:45,240
Just find any treasure
and you're automatically in the game.

12
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:50,740
Over three days, 300+ participants
and 100+ stands took part.

13
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:55,900
In our merch store, points buy rewards.
We had 200+ transactions.

14
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:58,800
Exhibitors get more interactions.

15
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:03,360
And because it's gamified,
people get really excited too.

16
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:08,040
We also let participants
hide their own treasures on the map,

17
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:13,140
expanding the game naturally
and keeping the gameplay lively.

18
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:17,940
Participants hid them in the bathrooms,
under tables and chairs,

19
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,680
on doors, even at the bus stop.

20
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:23,900
The whole app is built on the blockchain.

21
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,420
It runs on smart contracts.

22
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:31,520
You don't need any technical knowledge
to play the game.

23
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:37,920
But if you want to know more,
you can do that in the app,

24
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:40,600
and even see the code
behind the game.

25
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:46,900
On the map, a player sees the treasures
they've found and the ones still hidden.

26
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:51,820
Players can also go straight to the store
and see every product available,

27
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:56,600
and how many points
each one costs to redeem.

28
00:01:56,860 --> 00:02:02,540
This format works well not only at events
like trade fairs and expos,

29
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:08,060
but also on campuses, in companies,
or even across a whole city or town,

30
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:14,780
where we mark hidden treasures on the map,
and people claim their points.

31
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:18,560
Overall, the game energizes the conference,

32
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:22,810
driving more interaction
between attendees and the exhibition.

